The area measured by $\int_{-2}^{4}f(x)\,dx$ is estimated using $8$ strips of equal width, shown by the dashed lines.
Find $\Delta x$, and find the $x$-coordinate of the third boundary point, counting $x=-2$ as the first.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.55cm]
\fill[gray!35] (1,0) -- (1,1) -- plot[smooth,domain=1:9,variable=\x] ({\x},{sqrt(\x)}) -- (9,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.8,0) -- (10.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.6) -- (0,4.2) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,->,domain=0:10.2,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{sqrt(\x)});
\node at (6.6,3.3) {$y=\sqrt{x}$};
\foreach \x in {1,3,5,7,9} \draw (\x,0.12) -- (\x,-0.12) node[below] {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {1,2,3} \draw (0.2,\y) -- (-0.2,\y) node[left] {$\y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The shaded region is bounded by $y=\sqrt{x}$, the $x$-axis, $x=1$ and $x=9$.
Write its area first as a limit of a sum, then as a definite integral.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (-1,-3) -- plot[smooth,domain=-1:2,variable=\x] ({\x},{\x*\x-4}) -- (2,0) -- (-1,0) -- cycle;
\fill[gray!35] (2,0) -- plot[smooth,domain=2:3,variable=\x] ({\x},{\x*\x-4}) -- (3,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-3.4,0) -- (3.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
