The shaded region is divided into $n$ equal strips of width $\Delta x$.
Write $\Delta x$ in terms of $n$, and state what $\sum_{2}^{5}x^{2}\,\Delta x$ approaches as $n\to\infty$.

mastery.question_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- (0,3) -- (3,0) -- cycle;
\fill[gray!35] (3,0) -- (5,-2) -- (5,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.4,0) -- (6.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.4) -- (0,4.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,<->] (-1,4) -- (6,-3);
\node at (4,2) {$y=3-x$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} \draw (\x,0.12) -- (\x,-0.12) node[below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {-2,2} \draw (0.12,\y) -- (-0.12,\y) node[left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Without evaluating it, decide whether $\int_{0}^{5}(3-x)\,dx$ is positive, negative or zero, and justify your decision from the graph.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.5cm]
\fill[gray!35] (-3,0) -- (-3,1.5) -- plot[smooth,domain=-3:7,variable=\x] ({\x},{0.06*(\x+3)*(7-\x)+1.5}) -- (7,0) -- cycle;
\fill[gray!70] (1,0) -- (1,2.94) -- plot[smooth,domain=1:1.4,variable=\x] ({\x},{0.06*(\x+3)*(7-\x)+1.5}) -- (1.4,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-4.6,0) -- (8.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.4) -- (0,4.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,<->,domain=-4:8,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.06*(\x+3)*(7-\x)+1.5});
\node at (4.6,3.6) {$y=f(x)$};
\draw (-3,0.12) -- (-3,-0.12) node[below] {$-3$};
\draw (7,0.12) -- (7,-0.12) node[below] {$7$};
\draw[<->] (1,-0.6) -- (1.4,-0.6);
\node[below] at (1.2,-0.65) {$\Delta x=0.4$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A Riemann sum for $\int_{-3}^{7}f(x)\,dx$ uses strips of width $\Delta x=0.4$, one of which is shaded darker.
How many strips are there, and how many boundary points?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.5cm, y=0.3cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- (0,12) -- (6,0) -- cycle;
\fill[gray!35] (6,0) -- (10,-8) -- (10,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.6,0) -- (12,0) node[right] {$t$ (s)};
\draw[->] (0,-11) -- (0,15.5) node[above] {$v$ (m/s)};
\draw[thick,<->] (-1,14) -- (11,-10);
\node at (8,7) {$v=12-2t$};
\foreach \x in {2,4,6,8,10} \draw (\x,0.5) -- (\x,-0.5) node[below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\x$};
\foreach \y in {-8,-4,4,8,12} \draw (0.2,\y) -- (-0.2,\y) node[left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$\y$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A car's velocity $v$ metres per second over $0\le t\le 10$ seconds is graphed, with $v$ negative after $t=6$ because the car reverses.
Explain what $\int_{0}^{10}v\,dt$ measures, and why it is smaller than the total distance the car travels.
